# Cursor Agent Team Project Rules

## Overview
This is the Cursor Agent Team (CAT) framework, hosted primarily on Trae CN.
For full documentation, see the `cursor-agent-team` submodule.

## Core Roles
- **Discussion Partner**: Exploration mode - breadth and depth, no execution
- **Crew Member**: Execution mode - strict adherence to plan as specification
- **Prompt Engineer**: Creates and maintains new roles
- **Writer**: Executes prose plans with Draft -> Review -> Final quality control

## Workflow
1. **Plan**: Use discussion partner to explore ideas and generate execution plans
2. **Execute**: Use crew member to execute the plans
3. **Expand**: Use prompt engineer to create new roles when needed

## CAT Routing
- Role-mask rules are installed at `.trae/rules/` (`cat-router` is always on;
  the six mask rules activate on demand).
- Skills are installed at `.trae/skills/cursor-agent-team-*`.
- Trae CLI (`traecli`) reads AGENTS.md, `.trae/rules/` and `.trae/skills/`
  natively, so the same install serves both IDE and CLI.

## AI Workspace
All plans, notes, and discussion topics are stored in `cursor-agent-team/ai_workspace/`.

## Shared Workspace
This workspace is shared between Trae CN, Cursor and Claude Code.
